<!--Post: 171--><!--Time: 1086302219-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST171"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:webmaster@catchbtk.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Tom_voigt<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tom_voigt<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, June 03, 2004 - 3:36 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Aside from the multiple killings and writing of taunting letters for the news media to publish, here&#39;s the strongest evidence I can find that BTK was a Zodiac buff:  <BR>In September 1969, the Zodiac killer surprised a young couple and immediately brandished a guy to control the situation. Zodiac assured them it was simply a routine robbery and that he merely needed their money and car keys because he was wanted in another state and needed to escape. Once the victims were securely bound, Zodiac&#39;s true murderous intentions were quickly revealed.  <BR> <BR>During BTK&#39;s April 1974 Bright attack &#40;yes, I believe BTK was responsible&#41;, BTK immediately brandished a gun to control the situation and then attempted to put the victims at ease by assuring them it was only a routine robbery. BTK claimed he was wanted in another state and needed money and a car to flee. Once the victims were bound, BTK&#39;s true murderous intentions were quickly revealed.  <BR> <BR>Coincidence?  <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 171-->
<!--Post: 402--><!--Time: 1089316130-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST402"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Warren_b<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Warren_b<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, July 08, 2004 - 12:48 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->And I think he said he was going to California?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 402-->
<!--Post: 404--><!--Time: 1089344565-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST404"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Laoise<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Laoise<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, July 08, 2004 - 8:42 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->In &#39;74 how much of that &#39;69 zodiac case had been published?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 404-->
<!--Post: 405--><!--Time: 1089344815-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST405"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Matt<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Matt<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, July 08, 2004 - 8:46 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Have the cops done any cross referencing of california males who traded in calif. driver&#39;s licenses for kansas licenses those years???<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 405-->
<!--Post: 412--><!--Time: 1089429195-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST412"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:zodiacfiles@aol.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Ed_neil<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ed_neil<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, July 09, 2004 - 8:13 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Other than the usual newspaper accounts and magazine articles, there are two books that I know of published prior to 1975 that had chapters on the Zodiac case: <i>The California Crime Book</i> by Robert Colby &#40;1971&#41; and <i>Great Crimes of San Francisco: True Tales of Intrigue by the Bay</i>, edited by Dean W. Dickensheet &#40;1974&#41;.  Duffy Jennings &#40;who wrote many Z stories for the <i>SF Chronicle</i> in the 1970&#39;s&#41; wrote the chapter on Z in the latter book.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 412-->
<!--Post: 414--><!--Time: 1089435715-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST414"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Laoise<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Laoise<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, July 09, 2004 - 10:01 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->ok, but did said magazine articles, books ar newspaper articles mention Z saying that it was routine robbery etc? <BR> <BR>My opinion of BTK is that he&#39;s a copycat. Simple as that. I had thought that it was lame in unoriginal of him to do that, however my husband pointed out how absolutely smart that really is. Like he said, profilers look at the crimes and crime scenes to determine who theyre looking for right? Well, in this case, theyre profiling mainly one, with aspects of a few others, and none of them are actually BTK. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 414-->
<!--Post: 418--><!--Time: 1089472714-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST418"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:zodiacfiles@aol.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Ed_neil<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ed_neil<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, July 10, 2004 - 8:18 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->In both books, the Lake Berryessa attack is described in detail; Z initially demanded money and car keys, because he was an escaped convict from Montana and killed a guard there.  Then, part of his 11-9-1969 letter is quoted, where Z says he is angry about the police for telling lies about him, so he would change the way he collected his slaves for his afterlife by making some of his future murders look like &#34;routine robberies,&#34; among other things. <BR> <BR>So, Z didn&#39;t appear to have used that precise wording at LB, but he did in a letter a month and a half later.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 418-->
<!--Post: 430--><!--Time: 1089615071-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST430"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:webmaster@catchbtk.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Tom_voigt<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tom_voigt<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, July 11, 2004 - 11:51 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->In one of BTK&#39;s letters, he complained about a lack of publicity and listed between 15 and 17 other serial killers who were more famous than he. Any guesses who he left off the list?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 430-->
<!--Post: 448--><!--Time: 1089710655-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST448"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:zodiacfiles@aol.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Ed_neil<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ed_neil<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, July 13, 2004 - 2:24 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Here&#39;s some weird, possibly Z-related stuff: <BR> <BR>1&#41; The Zodiac had an apparent military, possibly Naval, background.  The Oteros lived on Edge<b>moor</b>; one <b>moors</b> a ship to land. <BR>Nancy Fox lived on S. Pershing.  General John Joseph Pershing was commander in chief of US forces in France in WWI. <BR> <BR>2&#41; The Zodiac had an apparent affinity for water.  His murders occurred at Lake Herman Road &#40;half a mile from Lake Herman&#41;, Blue Rock Springs &#40;about 100 feet from a sulphur spring&#41;, Lake Berryessa, and Washington Street &#40;although the last is a stretch&#41;.  Shirley Vian lived on S. Hydraulic &#40;of course, hydraulics deal with water&#41;. <BR> <BR>3&#41; In one Zodiac communication from 3-22-1971 &#40;the authenticity of which is not certain&#41;, there was a phrase on the card, &#34;peek through the <b>pines</b>.&#34; That precise phrase is specifically mentioned in the Zodiac chapter in <i>Great Crimes of San Francisco</i>.  BTK waited in a home on South <b>Pine</b>crest on 4-28-1979 to kill someone, but got tired of waiting and left. <BR> <BR>4&#41; The Zodiac appeared to harp on the number 13 four times: in the 4-20-1970 letter, he claimed to have encoded his name in a string of 13 cipher symbols, and claimed 13 victims in his letter of 7-26-1970 and a card on 10-5-1970  &#40;although I have doubts as to its authenticity, it was still published in the paper&#41;, and there were 13 eyes on a Halloween card he sent to <i>Chronicle</i> reporter Paul Avery on 10-27-1970.  BTK murdered Kathryn Bright on E. 13th, Vicki Wegerle was murdered on W. 13th, the family car was found in the 1300 block of North Edwards, and Shirley Vian&#39;s home was at 1311 S. Hydraulic; four 13s for BTK as well. <BR> <BR>5&#41; The number 17 was also important to the Zodiac.  Three of the four ciphers he sent to the papers were in columns of 17 characters, and his letter to the <i>LA Times</i> on 3-13-1971 claimed 17&#43; victims.  BTK listed 17 serial killers who were getting more attention than he was &#40;but did not mention the Zodiac&#41;. <BR> <BR>6&#41; Of course, the Zodiac wrote many letters to the police through the newspapers, as has BTK.  The Zodiac called the police twice after his murders to report them, and BTK did so at least once. <BR> <BR>7&#41; The Zodiac murdered David Faraday and Betty Lou Jensen on 12-20-1968, and mailed a letter to Melvin Belli asking for help on 12-20-1969.  Kathleen Johns was apparently abducted by the Zodiac and escaped on 3-22-1970, and the &#34;peek through the pines&#34; card was mailed on 3-22-1971 &#40;whether Z was involved or not, and whether the card is authentic or not is irrelevant, because they were considered so by Duffy Jennings in <i>Great Crimes of San Francisco</i>&#41;.  The Zodiac mailed a greeting card on 4-28-1970, and BTK&#39;s abortive murder was supposed to occur on 4-28-1979.  It&#39;s also interesting to note that Shirley Vian was murdered on 3-17-1977, and precisely 27 years later to the day on 3-17-2004, BTK mailed a letter to the <i>Eagle</i> containing a photocopy of Vicki Wegerle&#39;s driver&#39;s license.  While it was not publically known in 1977 &#40;as far as I know, but it was something I discovered and posted over at the zodiackiller.com message board a few years back&#41;, Zodiac victim Darlene Ferrin&#39;s birthday was March 17th. <BR> <BR>Now, maybe I&#39;m imagining things, but it certainly looks to me as if BTK studied the Z case through the newspapers and possibly <i>The California Crime Book</i> and <i>Great Crimes of San Francisco</i>.  And I believe he was astute and calculating enough to note these things to use in his own crimes. <BR> <BR>So... what do you all think?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 448-->
<!--Post: 449--><!--Time: 1089711754-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST449"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:webmaster@catchbtk.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Tom_voigt<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tom_voigt<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, July 13, 2004 - 2:42 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Ed, I&#39;m glad you&#39;re here and I agree that BTK was highly influenced by the Zodiac. Great post and keep it up.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 449-->
<!--Post: 450--><!--Time: 1089712179-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST450"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:webmaster@catchbtk.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Tom_voigt<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tom_voigt<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, July 13, 2004 - 2:49 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->By the way, the Zodiac case was covered quite nicely by the wire services in the Wichita area back in the 1970s.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 450-->
<!--Post: 451--><!--Time: 1089712289-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST451"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:zodiacfiles@aol.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Ed_neil<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ed_neil<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, July 13, 2004 - 2:51 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Thanks, Tom.  It sure as hell looks like BTK used the Zodiac case to pattern his own crimes after.  It doesn&#39;t take a rocket scientist to see that BTK idolizes the Zodiac.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 451-->
<!--Post: 452--><!--Time: 1089716845-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST452"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, July 13, 2004 - 4:07 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Ed, your list, off the top of my head. The number 13. Some people <BR>will deliberately choose the number 13 for a jersey, a lottery number or what have you. Taken to an extreme, I could swear there is/was a &#34;society&#34; of people who gathered each Friday the 13th and I guess laughed at all who suffered from triskaidekaphobia, or fear of the number 13. <BR>Did Wichita have a chapter of these scoffers of the &#34;bad luck&#34; the number 13 &#34;caused?&#34; Bookworm, good soul, have you any reference to the &#34;society&#34; or &#34;club&#34; I mention? <BR> <BR>There&#39;s also the number 17, as in March 17, of course. St. Patty&#39;s Day and, say, Halloween are each &#34;unofficial&#34; holidays. I don&#39;t think the Vian and Wegerle 3/17 dates are coincidental.  <BR>I think BTK was clearly trying to do his best Zodiac imitation. <BR> <BR>Finally, one of my own: the simple fact of how very rare American serial killers who communicate with the media are. <BR>Zodiak and BTK are two of what, four or five? &#40;Or fewer.&#41; <BR>Nice post. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 452-->
<!--Post: 455--><!--Time: 1089739731-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST455"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:zodiacfiles@aol.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Ed_neil<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ed_neil<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, July 13, 2004 - 10:28 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->George: I&#39;m still getting up to speed on BTK, but I&#39;ve studied the Z case for more than 11 years now &#40;which is why I&#39;m obviously so familiar with it&#41;.  I was going over the timeline again last night, and noticed a few Z-like things, and the more I looked, the more there were. <BR> <BR>The &#34;society&#34; you&#39;re thinking of is the &#34;Eccentrics Club.&#34;  They meet every Friday the 13th and defy every superstition there is.  I don&#39;t know if Wichita had/has a chapter, however.  The only place I&#39;d heard of this club is the 1976 Reader&#39;s Digest book, <i>Strange Stories, Amazing Facts</i> &#40;p. 281&#41;. <BR> <BR>Another number I noticed that may be significant to BTK is 3 and/or 9.  The Zodiac mailed a <a href="http://www.zodiackiller.com/DragonCard.html" target="_blank">greeting card</a> to the <i>Chronicle</i> on 4-28-1970, and BTK&#39;s abortive murder attempt on S. Pinecrest occurred precisely 9 &#40;3x3&#41; years later to the day on 4-28-1979.  Then, 27 &#40;3x9 or 3x3x3&#41; years to the day after the murder of Shirley Vian on 3-17-1977, BTK mailed a letter to the <i>Eagle</i>.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 455-->
<!--Post: 456--><!--Time: 1089741155-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST456"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:zodiacfiles@aol.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Ed_neil<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ed_neil<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, July 13, 2004 - 10:52 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->And here&#39;s another parallel that just occurred to me: the Zodiac took Paul Stine&#39;s wallet, tore off his shirt tail, and took the cab&#39;s keys on 10-11-1969 after shooting him in the head.  Obviously, Stine&#39;s driver&#39;s license was in his wallet.  BTK took Vicki Wegerle&#39;s driver&#39;s license.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 456-->
<!--Post: 461--><!--Time: 1089777061-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST461"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Unsub<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Unsub<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, July 13, 2004 - 8:51 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Just to add some info here..the information made available to the public only lists 5 SK names Jack the Ripper, The Boston Strangler,Harvey Glatman, The Pantyhose Strangler and Ted from the West Coast. This is from memory so if I am off forgive me. During the Dateline NBC piece, Ron Lowen, the newsman who received the letter stated he had named 15-17 serial killers and wanted &#34;to be in the serial killer Hall of Fame&#34;. My point being that between the known and unknown names in the letter we have a gap of 10-12 names of which Zodiac could very well be one. <BR> <BR>As for media sources, with his tastes I bet BTK got alot of his info from the &#34;True Detective&#34; style magazines, I am willing to bet Zodiac got plenty of coverage in them. Other things point to this as well, he is familiar with lesser known killers perhaps not carried via the wire service and if you look at the names he suggests for himself in his letter they look like the titles they use for stories in these types of magazines.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 461-->
<!--Post: 462--><!--Time: 1089777673-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST462"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:webmaster@catchbtk.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Tom_voigt<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tom_voigt<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, July 13, 2004 - 9:01 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Unsub, I have about the best possible source you can imagine on this and he told me that BTK did not mention Zodiac.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 462-->
<!--Post: 463--><!--Time: 1089778105-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST463"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Flytodeb<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Flytodeb<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, July 13, 2004 - 9:08 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Everyone, I have always thought BTK began killing because he wanted to do it just like the Zodiac, only bigger and better in his own twisted mind. One instance of copy cat that perhaps hasn&#39;t been mentioned: I read that the Zodiac did not acknowledge the Riverside murder for many years. Vickie Wegerle was the 1986 victim that BTK never acknowledged until 2004. She lived at 2404 W. 13th St., the only victim who lived on the west side of Wichita, near the Arkansas River. &#34;Riverside&#34;? <BR>-Deb <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 463-->
<!--Post: 464--><!--Time: 1089780276-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST464"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:zodiacfiles@aol.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Ed_neil<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ed_neil<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, July 13, 2004 - 9:44 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Deb: this is exactly what we&#39;re after here.  It&#39;s possible that some of what I found is a bit of a stretch, but when one starts finding more than just one or two parallels, well, you know what they say about where there&#39;s smoke.  I had little interest in BTK until recently &#40;after all, the Zodiac is keeping us pretty busy here in the Bay Area&#41;, but now, I see that BTK has apparently modelled himself after Z and now deserves much closer scrutiny.  In fact, I wouldn&#39;t be surprised if BTK is doing a lot of the things Z is often accused of doing, such as encoding his name in his letters, among other things.  In other words, there may be far more to BTK&#39;s pattern of crimes than meets the eye...<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 464-->
<!--Post: 465--><!--Time: 1089780577-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST465"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:zodiacfiles@aol.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Ed_neil<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ed_neil<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, July 13, 2004 - 9:49 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Something else I thought of today: perhaps BTK targeted Shirley Vian because her name could be a play on words and an anagram that describes him: perhaps he is &#34;surely vain.&#34;<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 465-->
<!--Post: 471--><!--Time: 1089799229-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST471"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, July 14, 2004 - 3:00 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Unsub: I believe H.H. Holmes &#40;birth name: Herman Mudgett&#41; was another name BTK used in one of his letters. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 471-->
<!--Post: 472--><!--Time: 1089799626-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST472"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, July 14, 2004 - 3:07 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Thanks Ed for the &#34;Eccentrics Club&#34; information. A bit of a moon shot on my part, I admit. <BR> <BR>And the number 17, rather the date, 3/17 is not a reference to Mr. Penn is any way, shape or form. <BR> <BR>I agree with Tom that there may be &#40;I think there are/were&#41; communiques from BTK to media which WPD either has censored entirely or missed.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 472-->
<!--Post: 484--><!--Time: 1089834272-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST484"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:zodiacfiles@aol.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Ed_neil<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ed_neil<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, July 14, 2004 - 12:44 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->George: you are correct, 17 has nothing to do with Gareth Penn&#39;s atrocious book, <i>Times 17: The Amazing Story of the Zodiac Murders in California and Massachussetts, 1966-1981</i>.  17 is a number that was important to the Zodiac.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 484-->
<!--Post: 487--><!--Time: 1089886441-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST487"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Laoise<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Laoise<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, July 15, 2004 - 3:14 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Z wrote: &#34;they shall look like routine robberies, killings of anger, &amp; a few fake accidents, etc&#34; <BR> <BR>BTK wrote: &#34;You guess the motive and the victims.&#34; <BR> <BR>Z wrote: &#34;as of yet i have left no fingerprints behind me contrary to what the police say&#34; <BR> <BR>As far as I know, there was only one partial print left behind by BTK and that was on a chair in Nancy Fox&#39;s home, I believe. <BR> <BR>z said he didnt look anything at all like he did when he killed but he wouldnt say what he did look like.... btk could very well have been wearing a good wig type thing to darken his hair... that would also explain the knit cap pulled down low that kevin bright remembers. <BR> <BR>Z wrote: &#34;i would have sent you pictures but you would be nasty enough to trace them back to the develeper&#34; etc <BR> <BR>BTK is thought to have taken pics and possibly audio recorded the kills... pics are believed to be polaroids....no developer involved... so a student of Z even at that time? <BR> <BR>In the april 20th letter, Z said he didnt bomb some cop... reminicient of btk and the alleged letter after the fager murders in 1986. Granted that letter has never been a confirmed BTK communique but I am inclined to believe it was... <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 487-->
<!--Post: 489--><!--Time: 1089896216-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST489"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Flytodeb<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Flytodeb<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, July 15, 2004 - 5:56 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Nice comparison, Laoise. The fingerprint was on the chair at the Otero home.  <BR>-Deb<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 489-->
<!--Post: 495--><!--Time: 1089930288-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST495"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:zodiacfiles@aol.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Ed_neil<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ed_neil<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, July 15, 2004 - 3:24 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->On one of BTK&#39;s letters, the return address was: <BR> <BR>Thomas B. King <BR>408 Clayton ST <BR>Wichita, KS 67203 <BR> <BR>Of course, the sender&#39;s initials are an anagram for BTK, but the street number, 408, is the same as the total number of cipher symbols in the Zodiac&#39;s first three-part cipher, sent to the <a href="http://www.zodiackiller.com/VTHCipher.html" target="_blank"><i>Vallejo Times-Herald</i></a>, the <a href="http://www.zodiackiller.com/ChronicleCipher.html" target="_blank"><i>SF Chronicle</i></a>, and the <a href="http://www.zodiackiller.com/ExaminerCipher.html" target="_blank"><i>SF Examiner</i></a>.  In Z&#39;s 6-26-1970 <a href="http://www.zodiackiller.com/ZButtonLetter.html" target="_blank">letter</a>, he included an <a href="http://www.zodiackiller.com/ZMap.html" target="_blank">inset map</a> section from a Phillips 66 road map that showed the Bay Area, and drew a &#34;magnetic indicator&#34; around Mt. Diablo.  This was essentially a clock-like symbol, with the numbers 0 &#40;instead of 12&#41;, 3, 6, and 9 spaced 90º apart.  Z drew an arrowhead to indicate north, and there is the name of a city that lies between the tip of that arrow and the 0: Clayton.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 495-->
<!--Post: 496--><!--Time: 1089930944-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST496"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:zodiacfiles@aol.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Ed_neil<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ed_neil<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, July 15, 2004 - 3:35 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->In the first of BTK&#39;s recent letters &#40;3-17-2004&#41;, the return address was: <BR> <BR><b>Bill</b> Thomas <b>Kill</b>man <BR>1684 S. Oldmanor <BR>Wichita, KS 67218 <BR> <BR>Of course, the sender&#39;s initials are BTK, but the names I put in bold are <a href="http://imdb.com/title/tt0266697/" target="_blank"><i>Kill Bill</i></a>, a 2003 Quentin Tarantino movie.  Z made apparent movie references in his letters, such as 1932&#39;s <a href="http://imdb.com/title/tt0023238/" target="_blank"><i>The Most Dangerous Game</i></a> in his 408-cipher, and a specific reference to 1973&#39;s <a href="http://imdb.com/title/tt0069762/" target="_blank"><i>Badlands</i></a> in his 5-8-1974 <a href="http://www.zodiackiller.com/CitizenLetter.html" target="_blank">letter</a>.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 496-->
<!--Post: 499--><!--Time: 1089942202-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST499"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:zodiacfiles@aol.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Ed_neil<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ed_neil<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, July 15, 2004 - 6:43 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->BTK directed reporters to a photocopied letter in October 1974, which was placed in a mechanical <b>engineering</b> textbook at the Wichita Public Library.  According to <i>Zodiac</i> &#40;p. 142&#41;, Z might have been a British <b>engineer</b>; the incident related in the book occurred on 4-19-1970, but I have not been able to find any references to it in the Z stories I&#39;ve collected over the years, so I&#39;m not certain the engineering angle is anything more than coincidence at this point, unless someone finds a story that mentions it that BTK could have had access to prior to October 1974.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 499-->
<!--Post: 501--><!--Time: 1089968067-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST501"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, July 16, 2004 - 1:54 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Zodiac&#39;s 408 cipher speaks of sexual release. <BR> <BR>BTK speaks of sexual release with Shirley Vian&#39;s daughter in one of his letters.  <BR> <BR>I believe BTK covers the topic &#40;release&#41; again in a separate letter. I&#39;ll try to go check.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 501-->
<!--Post: 515--><!--Time: 1090229762-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST515"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:zodiacfiles@aol.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Ed_neil<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ed_neil<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, July 19, 2004 - 2:36 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->OK, I was perusing the <a href="http://p216.ezboard.com/fcrimeandjustice13552frm100.showMessage?topicID=456.topic" target="_blank">C&amp;J BTK threads</a> &#40;7th post, by spud on 7-17 at 7:22 PM&#41;, and there I found that when BTK called and directed reporters to his letter of October 1974, the actual date was 10-22-1974, precisely five years to the day after someone claiming to be the Zodiac called Oakland PD and demanded that F. Lee Bailey or Melvin Belli appear on Jim Dunbar&#39;s show later that morning.  Apparently, this is the first time the actual date of that letter was mentioned. <BR> <BR>If I had any doubts before about BTK being a student of Z, I don&#39;t have any now.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 515-->
<!--Post: 516--><!--Time: 1090230683-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST516"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:zodiacfiles@aol.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Ed_neil<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ed_neil<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, July 19, 2004 - 2:51 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->In addition to the 17 serial killers BTK listed, he mailed his first known letter in 25 years on March 17th, and if this package found at the Wichita Public Library turns out to be from BTK, he obviously intended it to be found on July 17th.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 516-->
<!--Post: 528--><!--Time: 1090307364-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST528"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Sandy<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Sandy<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, July 20, 2004 - 12:09 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Ed,Don&#39;t forget that at the Lake Herman rd. Dec. 20th 68 shooting,there was a sign on a pole at that site with a large number &#34;3&#34; on it. It has been removed,but I believe I might have a picture of it taken in 1990. The other thing that I find very interesting is, BTK is about the same age as Zodiac,I wonder how he was able to even copy that? Maybe he and Zodiac were close friends, while btk was living in Calif? On Dec.18th 1970 In Contra Costa Co. a man wareing a navy blue &#34;knit cap&#34; tape on his finger tips, broke into a home ,carrying  a baseball bat,&#40;a silent weapon&#41; the woman in the home grabbed her shot gun,the man left leaving only a palm print in blood. Police thought he could have been the Zodiac. BTK also wore a knit cap, it is called a &#34;watch&#34;mans cap. Time was very important to the Zodiac,BTK took Mr.Otero&#39;s watch.The thing that bugs me is ,if he wanted to be so much like the Zodiac,why didn&#39;t he kill people in cars ? Better yet, why not just claim to be the Zodiac ? He would have gotten far more attention doing that I would think.I think it is very strange indeed, that BTK didn&#39;t mention the Zodiac.Sometimes it is what a person leaves out,that could be very important!<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 528-->
<!--Post: 532--><!--Time: 1090372493-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST532"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, July 20, 2004 - 6:14 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text--><i>Alleged</i> Zodiac victim Kathleen Johns, very pregnant and with a toddler in tow, <i>allegedly</i> leaped from a moving car &#40;depending upon which of the fifty versions of her story you happen to have heard&#41; and ended up without having suffered any serious injury. The date was 3/20/70. <BR> <BR>A Potential BTK victim also had luck on her side. <BR>On 4/28/79 the 63 year-old woman whom BTK had planned to attack, was saved by the simple fact that BTK grew tired of waiting for her to return home.  <BR> <BR>When the Kathleen Johns story hit the papers and the ever-opportunistic Zodiac claimed responsibility for the crime in a letter, <BR><a href="http://www.zodiackiller.com/JohnsLetter.html" target=_top>http://www.zodiackiller.com/JohnsLetter.html</a>  <BR>as well as in the letter below, albeit more obliquely. The below link leads to a Zodiac missive which grotesquely parodies a Gilbert and Sullivan song, especially pages 2,3,4, and 5. <BR><a href="http://www.zodiackiller.com/Mikado2.html" target=_top>http://www.zodiackiller.com/Mikado2.html</a> <BR> <BR> BTK would have believed Johns a genuine Zodiac victim. It&#39;s a stretch but perhaps the 63 year-old was BTK&#39;s version of Kathleen Johns?  <BR> <BR>Having said that, I&#39;ll also say that if Johns was a Zodiac victim, then so was Marilyn Monroe. Johns as a Zodiac victim probably makes my top five when it comes to asinine beliefs concerning the Zodiac crimes. <BR>Anyway, because the papers would have presented Johns as a genuine Zodiac victim, perhaps BTK wanted his own version of such a woman as well? <BR> <BR>PS: I&#39;m not making light of a scary ordeal which I do believe happened to the late Kathleen Johns. <BR>My only point is my belief that Zodiac was <b>not</b> the man who drove her all over the place and frightened her. I base this on the fact that the unfortunate Ms. Johns was incapable of keeping even the most basic of facts straight &#40;she identified more than one man as her abductor, for example&#41; and frankly  <BR>her memory was all but shot. On a witness stand, a layperson could have caught her in a couple of dozen contradictions. If you want any more info on Kathleen Johns, you&#39;ll find it at Tom&#39;s Zodiac site. I sympathize with KJ and some believe she was indeed kidnapped by the Zodiac. I simply disagree with their point of view. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 532-->
<!--Post: 566--><!--Time: 1090803439-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST566"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, July 25, 2004 - 5:57 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Ed, <BR>As you say, BTK lead reporters to a mechanical engineering textbook. <BR> <BR>In a Zodiac letter, on this page, <a href="http://www.zodiackiller.com/Mikado5.html" target=_top>http://www.zodiackiller.com/Mikado5.html</a> <BR> <BR>Zodiac uses a term we&#39;ve seen several thousand times: Radian. <BR> <BR>The group of professionals most associated with the term &#34;radian&#34; are, of course, <u>engineers.</u> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 566-->
<!--Post: 578--><!--Time: 1090816206-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST578"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Laoise<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Laoise<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, July 25, 2004 - 9:30 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Otero&#39;s car was a &#39;66 <BR>Wegerle&#39;s car was a &#39;79 <BR> <BR>Now, Im gonna go out on a limb here and say what ive been thinking: Its my understanding that Z wrote a letter in &#39;79 that hadnt been discovered until a year ago right? So the only way that BTK could have possibly known about the &#39;79 letter thereby using that year as a connection in the Wegerle killing is if he had actually been in contact with Z or someone who had seen the letter already. At first, you might think this improbable, until you work out dates and make a huge assumption. If Arthur Lee Allen were in fact Z, and BTK were in the Navy with him that would have made BTK 18 at the time of joining the Navy, 36 in &#39;74 and 66 now.... see how I just made a turn around back to the year CJB was killed? <BR>Also, someone pointed out to me that all BTK&#39;s vics names end in an &#34;ee&#34; sound: Julie &#40;Otero&#41;, Shirley &#40;Vian&#41;, Nancy &#40;Fox&#41;, Vicki &#40;Wegerle&#41; and even Kathy if you were to indeed give credit for Kathryn Bright to BTK and shorten her name. Did that &#34;ee&#34; sounding connection come from Cheri &#40;CJB of course&#41;?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 578-->
<!--Post: 580--><!--Time: 1090818970-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST580"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Laoise<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Laoise<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, July 25, 2004 - 10:16 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Correction- &#39;78 letter and &#39;78 Monte Carlo is what wegerle drove.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 580-->
<!--Post: 582--><!--Time: 1090822581-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST582"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:zodiacfiles@aol.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Ed_neil<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ed_neil<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, July 25, 2004 - 11:16 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->George: good point.  However, it&#39;s also a mathematical term, and can therefore legitimately point to Mike O&#39;Hare or Ted Kaczinsky as Zodiac suspects.  What I&#39;m at a loss to explain so far is how BTK chose that particular type of book with no mention that I know of prior to 1986 concerning Z being an engineer.  So far, I think it was just a random choice &#40;but I still have a few newspapers to dig through as soon as I get the chance&#41;. <BR> <BR>Laoise: That Z letter from April 1978 was a hoax &#40;I&#39;ve long suspected it was the work of Robert Graysmith as I outlined in the <a href="http://www.zodiackiller.com/discus/messages/12/100.html#POST3150" target="_blank">Doubts as to the authenticity of all Z letters</a> discussion at zodiackiller.com&#39;s message board&#41;, and the recent discovery from LAPD&#39;s files last year was of a letter apparently written by Z to Channel 9 in May 1978.  Either way, the hoax letter was in the news for a time, and that was a few months before Wegerle&#39;s murder, so BTK could very easily have read about it.  Also, Wegerle&#39;s car was found parked in the <b>13</b>00 block of North Edwards, and 13 is a number that Z was apparently fond of.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 582-->
<!--Post: 588--><!--Time: 1090878098-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST588"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, July 26, 2004 - 2:41 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Ed, <BR>I&#39;d thought the term &#34;radian&#34; from Zodiac&#39;s &#34;Little List/Mikado&#34; letter had been published early enough for BTK to see the word &#39;radian&#39;. If so, and BTK wanted to imitate the Zodiac, an engineering book or a mathematical textbook would be appropriate places for BTK to place hs letter, as either textbook probably also contained the term radian. <BR> <BR>I had thought the BTK letter instructing reporters to the library and hence the engineering book was a 1974 letter. If BTK had seen the word &#34;radian&#34; in the Zodiac letter above, he may have looked up the word, seen what it was associated with, and placed it under/in the engineering textbook at the WSU library. Not only would this have been homage to Zodiac, but would have made BTK appear a real &#39;somebody&#39; who was involved with engineering or higher mathematics.  <BR>&#40;I could have sworn that the BTK letter which sent reporters to WSU library was a 1974 letter -- now I just checked at the C&amp;J board and notice BTK&#39;s letters are usually referred to as &#34;A letter was received&#34; and a month and a year are given. Other than the &#34;Curley Locks&#34; letter and a mention of an only-the-killer-would-know letter re: the Oteros, it appears that WPD is keeping things as censored as possible.  <BR> <BR> <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 588-->
<!--Post: 589--><!--Time: 1090878444-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST589"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, July 26, 2004 - 2:47 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Oops, <BR>Ed, I see it was a 1974 letter, from your post in this thread. The Mikado letter, the contents, weren&#39;t made public until after 1974? My bad on that one!<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 589-->
<!--Post: 650--><!--Time: 1091176745-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST650"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:zodiacfiles@aol.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Ed_neil<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ed_neil<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, July 30, 2004 - 1:39 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I&#39;ve been wondering why BTK mailed his first letter in 25 years on 3-17-2004.  Obviously, the reasons are fourfold: it&#39;s Darlene Ferrin&#39;s birthday, Ethan Allen &#40;Art Allen&#39;s father&#41; died on that day 33 years earlier, it was 27 years &#40;3x3x3&#41; years to the day after the murder of Shirley Vian &#40;coincidentally, Darlene would have turned 30 the day Shirley was murdered&#41;, and it was the 17th day of the 3rd month. <BR> <BR>In that letter, he claimed Vicki Wegerle as a victim; she was murdered on 9-16-1986.  Therefore, that letter was mailed 17 years, 6 months and 1 day after his last known murder.  Once again, the numbers 3 &#40;3x2 = 6&#41; and 17 come into play. <BR> <BR>It wouldn&#39;t surprise me if BTK feels some sort of twisted spiritual connection to Z.  And seeing all these numbers come into play reminds me a lot of Gareth&#39;s Penn&#39;s bizarre mathematical theories &#34;proving&#34; that Mike O&#39;Hare is Z.  Maybe I&#39;m way off here, but BTK might own a copy of <i>Times 17</i> and studied it, and that might be the reason he waited so long to start communicating again: he&#39;s using it as kind of a model to show how intertwined his and Z&#39;s lives are.  It&#39;s just an idea...<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 650-->
<!--Post: 687--><!--Time: 1091544716-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST687"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bookworm<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bookworm<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, August 03, 2004 - 7:51 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->&#34;The fingerprint was on the chair at the Otero home.&#34; <BR> <BR>Ed, <BR>There was a bloody print found on Stine&#39;s cab. Witnesses saw Z&#39;s hair color. Maybe BTK left the print on purpose, as a Z-related message. Chair could mean C hair or see hair.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 687-->
<!--Post: 688--><!--Time: 1091546548-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST688"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bookworm<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bookworm<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, August 03, 2004 - 8:22 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Just an after thought. BTK could also have been trying to say &#34;chai&#40;red&#41;cab&#34; or &#40;Shared cab, which Z did&#41;. The Otero&#39;s were hispanic and&#40;I think&#41;don&#39;t some hispanics say &#34;sh&#34; as &#34;ch&#34;? <BR> <BR>The reverse of that, Cherry would be pronounced Sheri, like Cheri Bates name.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 688-->
<!--Post: 692--><!--Time: 1091634225-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST692"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bookworm<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bookworm<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, August 04, 2004 - 8:43 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->The Exorcist Letter was sent on 1/29/74, exactly 14 days after the Otero murders. I wonder if Z was identifying himself with these murders, if Zodiac actually had written this letter. <a href="http://www.zodiackiller.com/ExorcistLetter.html" target=_top>http://www.zodiackiller.com/ExorcistLetter.html</a>  Or maybe it was written by BTK. Two weeks is long enough time to get to San Francisco and mail the letter.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 692-->
<!--Post: 693--><!--Time: 1091634819-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST693"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bookworm<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bookworm<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, August 04, 2004 - 8:53 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Another afterthought is that Paul Stine&#39;s cab number was 912 similar to 1/29.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 693-->
<!--Post: 700--><!--Time: 1091808649-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST700"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bookworm<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bookworm<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, August 06, 2004 - 9:10 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->This site has an article on the background of The Exorcist. <a href="http://www.holtz.org/Library/Social%20Science/History/Atomic%20Age/Exorcist/Exorcist.htm" target=_top>http://www.holtz.org/Library/Social%20Science/Hist ory/Atomic%20Age/Exorcist/Exorcist.htm</a> <BR> <BR>The original diary of the exorcism began on January 15, 1949, the month and date of the Otero murders. <BR> <BR>The address of the boy who was possessed was 3807 40th Street, Cottage City &#40;near Washington DC&#41;. 40th Street had been at one time Central before it was changed. The Oteros car had been found on the corner of Oliver and Central. Also the Stine killing on the corner of Washington and Cherry was across from the address of 3898 Washington where witnesses lived. <BR> <BR>Seems to be a coincidence here?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 700-->
<!--Post: 701--><!--Time: 1091812703-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST701"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Scbenson2001<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Scbenson2001<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, August 06, 2004 - 10:18 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Bookworm, <BR> Having lived in the dc area most of my life, I know a little something about the background of this case. Almost all of it is urban myth. Including the boy&#39;s so called address. William Blatty based the story on a newspaper article he read while attending georgetown university. Although I have met people who swear they knew somebody who knew sombody who knew the priest did the so-called exorsism none of it is ever base on cold hard fact. I have done a little research on the internet on the case and people have come to the conclusion most of it was made up for the newspaper article that blatty read. He had no personal experience with the case other then reading the article.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 701-->
<!--Post: 722--><!--Time: 1092098937-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST722"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bookworm<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bookworm<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, August 09, 2004 - 5:48 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Concerning the Exorcist Letter, a new Exorcist movie is coming out on August 20th, this month.  <BR><a href="http://us.imdb.com/title/tt0204313/" target=_top>http://us.imdb.com/title/tt0204313/</a> <BR> <BR>Perhaps BTK&#39;s reappearance is timed for the movie. The initials of the last two return addresses are BTK and TBK. The author of the alleged exorcism diary was Father Albert Hughes. Initials FAH, corresponding alphabetic numbers of 618, move numbers as in TBK and you get 168 part of the return address. Hughes middle initial is E. or 5 just one off of 4 in the address. <BR> <BR>Address number for the first is 1684. In the July 31st cipher letters, Zodiac threatens more murder the weekend of Aug 1-69 or 8169. Move the letters around like TBK then you could have 1689 similar. The other address as Ed said is a reference to the 408 cipher. 804 is the reverse and the Monday after the weekend threat. <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 722-->
<!--Post: 727--><!--Time: 1092166138-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST727"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:zodiacfiles@aol.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Ed_neil<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ed_neil<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, August 10, 2004 - 12:28 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Now that I&#39;m thinking about it, Z mailed 3 letters on 4-30-1967 &#40;to the police, the paper, and CJB&#39;s father&#41;, 6 months to the day after the murder of Cherie Jo Bates in Riverside &#40;on 10-30-1966&#41;, apparently in response to a story in the local paper that same day with an update on her still-unsolved murder.  That was the only time we know of that Z mailed something on a 6-month anniversary.  It&#39;s also still debated as to whether he was the killer; a likely scenario is that he knew the killer, and decided to write the letters as a dry run for what he was planning in the Bay Area 2 years later.  In any case, CJB is still firmly part of the Z case, and so mailing the 3-17-2004 letter on that date brings in the number 17 &#40;as I mentioned above&#41;, but also in a sense is like the letters 6 months after CJB.  The reason he didn&#39;t mail them on the 16th is that the 17th was more important because of the Z case. <BR> <BR>Also, claiming Wegerle as a victim is like the <i>Chronicle</i> discovering that CJB was a Z victim 4 years after her murder; in this case, BTK had to connect himself to Wegerle because WPD never did. <BR> <BR>Of course, there was another letter on 6-17-2004, so once again, the number 17 comes into play for BTK.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 727-->
<!--Post: 728--><!--Time: 1092166841-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST728"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:zodiacfiles@aol.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Ed_neil<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ed_neil<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, August 10, 2004 - 12:40 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Another thing that I&#39;m thinking about is that Z mailed 3 letters on 4-30-1967, and 2 years, 3 months and 1 day later &#40;that is, 27 months later&#41;, mailed his first 3 letters as Z.  Maybe that&#39;s why BTK waited 27 years to the day after the murder of Shirley Vian to mail his first letter in 25 years.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 728-->
<!--Post: 734--><!--Time: 1092272721-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST734"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bookworm<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bookworm<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, August 11, 2004 - 6:05 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Regarding the Bates letters and the BTK recent correspondence address of 1684, Z July 31st threat/cipher letters had date  8/1/69, and alleged exorcism diary author Father Albert E. Hughes corresponding initials FAEH as 6158, all three have the numbers 168. The remaining numbers 495 correspond to alphabet letters &#34;DIE&#34; which was in all three Bates letters. <BR>  <BR>Another 168 is the 1year 6 months and 8 days between the murders of Snoozy and Furlong on Sunday, Aug 3rd, the weekend of the cipher letter threats and Kathy Bilek on April 11, 1971, just after the 3/13/71 Zodiac letter.  <BR>  <BR>The murderer, 18, was arrested &#40; Zodiac p.180 PB&#41; and said to have transferred from MA. &#34;early 1969 after the Zodiac murders began&#34; so he wasn&#39;t considered to be the Zodiac. I can&#39;t find the article anymore, but I think he was arrested on April 29, 1971. Pretty close to the month and day of the Bates letters 4/30. Also &#34;Christmass&#34; in the 3 cipher letters and Belli letter is spelled with the beginning of the name of Massachusettes. Could Z and BTK have known or known of this man &#40;Werner&#41;? <BR>  <BR>Marlborough is also near I-495 same numbers as the DIE above. I-495 encircles Washington, D.C. &#40;belt-way&#41; near the original alleged exorcism  the &#34;inspiration&#34; for the book and movie &#34;The Exorcist.&#34; <BR><a href="http://www.roadstothefuture.com/I495_VA_Desc.html" target=_top>http://www.roadstothefuture.com/I495_VA_Desc.html</a><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 734-->
<!--Post: 736--><!--Time: 1092277084-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST736"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, August 11, 2004 - 7:18 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->From birth to age 27, I lived inside the Beltway, I-495. Upper Marlboro &#40;spelled like the cigarette brand&#41;, is considered part the Washington, D.C. area &#40;Lower Marlboro isn&#39;t, at least I&#39;ve never heard it spoken as such&#41; and is in Prince George&#39;s County. It&#39;s, &#40;how can I phrase this?&#41;, not a safe area. However, at one time it was safe, if you go back to the first years of the 1970s and earlier -- and it may thus fit in. <BR> <BR>There are a lot of numbers moving around and simple coincidence, at some point, must be considered. That said, if anyone ever needs information about Zodiac or BTK and <i>any</i> sort of link to the D.C. area, please let me know, I can probably check out a few things after I&#39;ve arranged to borrow a car, which I can certainly do.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 736-->
<!--Post: 737--><!--Time: 1092278054-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST737"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, August 11, 2004 - 7:34 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text--><i>There are a lot of numbers moving around and simple coincidence, at some point, must be considered.</i> <BR> <BR>I refer to the specific I-495 and Upper Marlboro aspect only. <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 737-->
<!--Post: 742--><!--Time: 1092402403-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST742"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bookworm<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bookworm<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, August 13, 2004 - 6:06 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Hi George, <BR>I know the Oteros were from New York, but if Charley&#39;s recent interview was correct, Mr. Otero had a belt around his neck. Another possible coincidence. <BR> <BR>In the July 31st letters of Z, &#34;two&#34; of the dates are hyphenated like I-495. There was a double murder on Aug. 3rd &#40;Furlong and Snoozy&#41;. Then there was a single murder on April 11th &#40;Bilek&#41;. <BR> <BR>Chronicle &#34;1st of Aug, 69&#34; Envelope had 2 stamps-down <BR>Times Herald &#34;Aug 1-69&#34;  Envelope had 4 stamps-up <BR>Examiner &#34;Aug 1-69&#34;  Envelope had 2 stamps-up <BR> <BR>Could be a coincidence but the Times-Herald, Vallejo, Ca. had 4 stamps same as the number of Otero victims and Vallejo has all the Otero victims&#39; initials at the end of the name. Times-Herald has a hyphen. <BR> <BR> <BR> <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 742-->
<!--Post: 752--><!--Time: 1092494622-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST752"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bookworm<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bookworm<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, August 14, 2004 - 7:43 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Ed and George, <BR>There is an VA 27 Washington Boulevard and a &#34;Shirley Highway&#34; within the I-495 Beltway. I&#39;m thinking of Shirley Vian who was also strangled. &#34;via&#34; in latin means &#34;road, way, street.&#34; <a href="http://www.nd.edu/%7Earchives/vvv.htm" target=_top>http://www.nd.edu/%7Earchives/vvv.htm</a> <BR> <BR>&#34;the Mixing Bowl is the historic name for the interchange between I-395 Shirley Highway and VA-27 Washington Boulevard in Arlington, Virginia, near the Pentagon.&#34; <a href="http://www.roadstothefuture.com/Shirley_Highway.html" target=_top>http://www.roadstothefuture.com/Shirley_Highway.ht ml</a> <BR> <BR>I also found that there is more that one section of I-495 in several states. <BR><a href="http://www.kurumi.com/roads/3di/i495.html" target=_top>http://www.kurumi.com/roads/3di/i495.html</a> <BR> <BR>The difference between Marlborough and Marlboro is the end of the the first &#34;ugh&#34; H.G. is the initials of Henry G. Shirley, the highway namesake. <BR> <BR>Another BTK coincidence is that the ciphers/letters were given to &#34;Lynch&#34; Vallejo P.D. &#40;Zodiac PB p.50&#41;<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 752-->
<!--Post: 756--><!--Time: 1092495458-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST756"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Shyra<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Shyra<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->8-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, August 14, 2004 - 7:57 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Yes, Bookworm.  I am familiar with them as well.  What would you like to know?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 756-->
<!--Post: 767--><!--Time: 1092583261-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST767"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bookworm<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bookworm<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, August 15, 2004 - 8:21 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Hi Shyra, <BR>I&#39;m just speculating and putting some ideas/coincidences out for thought. The Washington D.C. aspect would be far-fetched except for the background on the Exorcist. <BR> <BR>Another coincidence with the date of Shirley Vians&#39;s death 3/17 is that the 3 cipher letters were sent on 7/31 just rearrangement of numbers. <BR> <BR>In Zodiac p. 53 &#40;footnote&#41; Graysmith says there were three stamps on the Chronicle cipher envelope. The scanned image only shows 2  <BR><a href="http://www.zodiackiller.com/ChronicleEnvelope.html" target=_top>http://www.zodiackiller.com/ChronicleEnvelope.html</a><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 767-->
<!--Post: 772--><!--Time: 1092633226-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST772"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:zodiacfiles@aol.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Ed_neil<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ed_neil<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, August 15, 2004 - 10:13 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Graysmith has been known to make the occasional error...<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 772-->
<!--Post: 782--><!--Time: 1092700111-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST782"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bookworm<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bookworm<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, August 16, 2004 - 4:48 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Hi Ed, <BR>Yes, Like Werner&#39;s name, just the paragraph before he put Warner. Maybe he was thinking about the officer on the Jensen/Faraday case, William T. Warner. <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 782-->
<!--Post: 881--><!--Time: 1093329271-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST881"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Superbike7<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Superbike7<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->8-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, August 23, 2004 - 11:34 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I think BTK is a big copy cat, but I think its  not just the zodiak he has copied . I also think he has taken things up to a new level more than any serial murder I have ever heard of. The Otero murders were jan 15 1974, the Black Delila murder was jan 15 1947.47 74 ? I am very frusturated that the Wichata pd has released so very little info to the public everything they have discovered  such as the o death song wsu connection I saw weeks ago on message boards.I think they are very worried about public panic so they are being very secretive. You cant control what BTK is going to do. I think Jacob Allens murder is BTKs Stine murder aka zodiak they have been very tight lipped about any info concerning Allens death. I do not think BTK is locked into any MO now all this time he has been able to refine his methods and I do not believe he always tells the truth such as Kathryn Brights murder its to his advantage to lie because he had an eye witness.I an sure this murder was his.Shame on you Wichita pd you havent been able to solve this case for 30 years.The public is your best ally to bring BTK to justice.Also to BTK if your reading this you are like a terrorist fear is what you get off on I am not afraid of you I think you are a sick weak person who when we find out who you are we will laugh and wonder so this is BTK A ordinary average man who only goes after the weak. I challenge you in Charlie Oteros words come after a man who has no family to protect, a man with nothing to lose one on one bring it on any time any place.I doubt you have the sack to do that.You always need an unfair advantage to do what you do I cant wait to see what a pathetic person you really are.One more thought I think he murdered before the Oteros possibly Sherry Baker<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 881-->
<!--Post: 882--><!--Time: 1093334818-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST882"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Superbike7<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Superbike7<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->8-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, August 24, 2004 - 1:06 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Correction,I didnt mean Sherry Baker it was a girl killed in the basement of the dorm at wsu. She was bound and stabbed several times about 1968.Also Bundy commited chi omega murders on Jan 15 1977.What is it about Jan 15th.I will post the name of the girl in 1968 when I find it.Sorry for the mistake.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 882-->
<!--Post: 899--><!--Time: 1093452620-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST899"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Micaela<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Micaela<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, August 25, 2004 - 9:50 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->You are possibly referring to Julie Ladd who was murdered at WSU in the basement in 1977. Now that is one case to really look into. There were so many similarities. But Leonard Bell confessed to that to avoid the death penalty for a murder he really did commit in Colorado. Did he do it? I doubt it. I think we will never know. It would be great Tom if you could actually speak with him. He is in a CO prison. If you want to know the phone and addy, let me know. <BR> <BR>Jaden<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 899-->
<!--Post: 1064--><!--Time: 1096365279-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1064"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:zodiacfiles@aol.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Ed_neil<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ed_neil<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, September 28, 2004 - 2:54 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->This weekend, I discovered that <i>Great Crimes of San Francisco: True Tales of Intrigue by the Bay</i> &#40;edited by Dean W. Dickensheet&#41; was originally published in December 1974. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1064-->
<!--Post: 1943--><!--Time: 1103154539-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1943"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Juno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Juno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, December 15, 2004 - 3:48 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Although I do not think he is Z, I would not be surprised if he frequents Zodiackiller.com, or did in the past.  I would have expected him to post there way before this site existed, actually.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1943-->
